---
/**
 * FutureSection — editorial vision statement for KeelHq.
 *
 * Responsibility:
 * - Render a large editorial block: left-aligned on mobile, centred on tablet+.
 */
---

<section class="future-section" aria-labelledby="future-heading">
  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <div class="landing-section">
    <div class="future-block" data-reveal>
      <p class="section-label">The Big Idea</p>
      <h2 id="future-heading" class="future-title">
        Your content should survive
        <span class="future-title__accent">
          redesigns.
          <svg
            class="future-title__underline"
            viewBox="0 0 160 16"
            preserveAspectRatio="none"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path
              d="M2 8 Q 80 16, 158 6"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="3"
              stroke-linecap="round"
            />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </h2>
      <p class="future-body">
        Most websites are rebuilt every time the design changes.
      </p>
      <p class="future-body" data-reveal style="transition-delay: 120ms">
        KeelHq separates your content from your design. That means you can:
      </p>
      <div class="future-cards" data-reveal style="transition-delay: 200ms">
        <div class="future-card">Generate a new website with AI</div>
        <div class="future-card">Switch frameworks</div>
        <div class="future-card">Refresh your branding</div>
        <div class="future-card">Completely redesign your frontend</div>
      </div>
      <p class="future-body" data-reveal style="transition-delay: 280ms">
        while keeping your content, media, forms, and data exactly where they belong.
      </p>
      <p class="future-body" data-reveal style="transition-delay: 360ms">
        Your website can change. Your content stays.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .future-section {
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .future-block {
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    text-align: left;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .future-block {
      max-width: 620px;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .future-block {
      max-width: 760px;
    }
  }

  .future-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-section-title);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .future-title__accent {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .future-title__underline {
    position: absolute;
    left: -4px;
    right: -4px;
    bottom: -6px;
    width: calc(100% + 8px);
    height: 14px;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .future-body {
    font-size: var(--font-size-section-sub);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-normal);
  }

  .future-cards {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .future-cards {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .future-card {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
